# Build context for the Containerfile. The wheel is built from
# `pyproject.toml`, `src/` and `README.md`, and its skill payload is
# force-included from `skill/` (see the wheel target below), so anything a
# developer machine carries beyond those only bloats the context or, worse,
# leaks foreign binaries into the image.

# Virtualenv and Python caches: a host venv holds a host-architecture
# interpreter that must never reach the image.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Everything the wheel does not need. The build reads `pyproject.toml`, `src/`,
# `README.md` and `skill/`: the last because
# [tool.hatch.build.targets.wheel.force-include] maps `skill/defold` into the
# package and hatchling resolves that source from the build context, so
# excluding it fails the build. The rest of the repository is documentation,
# tests and tooling that would only bloat the context.
tests/
docs/
openwiki/
.github/

# Version control and generated documentation state.
.git/
.gitignore

# Build outputs.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Local planning notes, if present.
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
